---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="SMS Terms & Privacy | Chiropractic Grit"
  description="SMS messaging terms of service and privacy policy for appointment reminders and notifications sent through Grit on behalf of healthcare providers."
>
  <Nav />

  <main class="page">
    <div class="container">

      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="page-header">
        <div class="kicker">SMS Terms & Privacy</div>
        <h1>SMS messaging terms.</h1>
        <p class="header-copy">
          Grit sends SMS messages on behalf of chiropractic practices for appointment reminders,
          confirmations, and practice notifications. This page describes how SMS messaging works,
          how consent is collected, and your rights.
        </p>
        <p class="last-updated">Last updated: March 30, 2026</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Content -->
      <div class="legal-content">

        <section>
          <h2>1. What messages will I receive?</h2>
          <p>
            When you opt in to SMS notifications from your chiropractic practice, you may receive:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Appointment reminders (e.g., "Your appointment is tomorrow at 2:00 PM")</li>
            <li>Appointment confirmations and scheduling updates</li>
            <li>Practice notifications (e.g., office closures, schedule changes)</li>
            <li>Balance and billing notifications</li>
            <li>Replies to messages you send to the practice</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Messages are sent on behalf of your healthcare provider's practice. Message frequency varies
            based on your appointment schedule and practice communications. Typically 2-8 messages per month.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. How consent is collected</h2>
          <p>
            You will only receive SMS messages after providing your consent through one of the following methods:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Patient portal</strong> — Opting in through your account settings or during registration</li>
            <li><strong>In-office</strong> — Providing written or verbal consent at your practice</li>
            <li><strong>Text reply</strong> — Replying YES or START to a consent request</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Your consent is recorded with a timestamp and the method used. Consent is specific to the
            practice you opted in with — opting in at one practice does not opt you in at another.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. How to opt out</h2>
          <p>
            You can stop receiving SMS messages at any time by:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Replying <strong>STOP</strong> to any message</li>
            <li>Updating your preferences in your patient portal account</li>
            <li>Contacting your practice directly</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            After opting out, you will receive a single confirmation message and no further texts will
            be sent. You can opt back in at any time by replying <strong>START</strong> or through your
            patient portal.
          </p>
          <p>
            Opting out of SMS does not affect your ability to use the secure patient portal or receive
            in-app messages from your provider.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. Help</h2>
          <p>
            Reply <strong>HELP</strong> to any message for assistance. You can also contact your practice
            directly or email us at <a href="mailto:support@chiropracticgrit.com">support@chiropracticgrit.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Message & data rates</h2>
          <p>
            Message and data rates may apply depending on your mobile carrier and plan. Grit does not
            charge patients for SMS messages, but your carrier's standard messaging rates apply.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. Privacy & PHI</h2>
          <p>
            SMS messages sent through Grit are limited to non-clinical content. We do not send
            protected health information (PHI) such as diagnoses, test results, or treatment details
            via text message. For private medical communications, your provider uses the secure
            patient portal.
          </p>
          <p>
            Your phone number is stored securely and is only used for practice communications
            you have consented to. We do not sell, share, or use your phone number for marketing
            purposes unrelated to your healthcare provider.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Supported carriers</h2>
          <p>
            SMS messaging is supported on all major US carriers including AT&T, T-Mobile, Verizon,
            and Sprint, as well as most regional carriers. Carriers are not liable for delayed or
            undelivered messages.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. Changes to these terms</h2>
          <p>
            We may update these terms from time to time. Changes will be reflected on this page with
            an updated date. Continued use of SMS services after changes constitutes acceptance of the
            revised terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="contact-section">
          <h2>9. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            For questions about SMS messaging, privacy, or to request opt-out assistance:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Email: <a href="mailto:support@chiropracticgrit.com">support@chiropracticgrit.com</a></li>
            <li>Or contact your practice directly</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

      </div>

    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    padding: 52px 0 84px;
  }

  .page-header {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin-bottom: 52px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .kicker {
    color: var(--ember);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 4.5vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .header-copy {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .last-updated {
    color: var(--subtle);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .legal-content {
    max-width: 740px;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  section:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }

  p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 10px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  li::before {
    content: '';
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--ember);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--ember);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  a:hover {
    color: var(--ember-strong);
  }

  strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .page {
      padding: 36px 0 64px;
    }

    section {
      margin-bottom: 28px;
      padding-bottom: 28px;
    }
  }
</style>
